.TH FROST 1 "2026" "frost" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
frost \- small terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frost
[\fB+\fILINE\fR] [\fIFILE\fR[\fB:\fILINE\fR]]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
A small editor for the terminal: menu bar and tabs like Fresh, keys like micro (CUA clipboard, mouse, multiple cursors).
It uses the colours of your terminal. It opens files of several gigabytes at once and keeps an unlimited undo history.
.PP
Without arguments frost restores the previous session: open tabs, cursors, unsaved and untitled text, closed tabs and undo history.
With file arguments it opens only those files and leaves the saved session alone, so it is safe as $EDITOR and $VISUAL (git, nnn, crontab).
.PP
When another program changes a file that is open, frost notices within about a second.
A tab without unsaved edits reloads (undo goes back).
A tab with unsaved edits is left alone and the status bar says so; saving then writes the text next to the file as
.I NAME.frost-mine
and leaves the changed file untouched.
Files over 4 MB are not followed.
.SH KEYS
.TP
Ctrl-S, Ctrl-Q, Ctrl-O, Ctrl-N, Ctrl-W
save, quit, open, new, close tab
.TP
Ctrl-Z, Ctrl-Y, Ctrl-X, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-V
undo, redo, cut, copy, paste
.TP
Ctrl-F, F3, Ctrl-H, Ctrl-G
find, find next, replace all, go to line
.TP
Ctrl-D, Alt-A, Alt-S, Ctrl-U, Alt-L, Alt-Up, Alt-Down
next occurrence as a new cursor, all occurrences, skip one, drop the newest cursor, cursor at the end of each selected line, cursor above, cursor below
.TP
Alt-., Alt-,, Alt-1 .. Alt-9, Alt-0
next tab, previous tab, tab number N, last tab (Ctrl-PgDn and Ctrl-PgUp also move)
.TP
Ctrl-T, Ctrl-L, Ctrl-P, F2, F1, F10
reopen closed tab, language, command palette, define word, keys, menu
.PP
F1 opens the key panel: every action with its keys.
Type to filter, Enter then a key rebinds the row, Insert adds a key, Delete unbinds, Ctrl-R restores the default.
Changes are saved to keys.lua.
.SH BRACKETS AND INDENTATION
Opening brackets and quotes get their partner as you type (per language; see docs/brackets.md), a closer typed in front of the same closer steps over it, Enter indents like the file does and opens a pair into three lines.
Unclosed brackets are underlined in red and reported in the status line.
Lisp is strict: an edit that would unbalance the brackets is refused.
Options: frost.auto_pair, frost.pairs[language], frost.strict[language].
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/frost/init.lua
configuration in Lua (theme, options, key bindings)
.TP
~/.config/frost/keys.lua
key bindings changed in the F1 panel (read after init.lua)
.TP
~/.config/frost/dictionary.txt
extra dictionary entries, one per line: word, TAB, meaning
.TP
~/.local/state/frost/
session and history
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/Gucixdev/frost
